{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning minimal local pytest shim**\n\n**Evaluating minimal pytest shim feasibility**\n\n**Considering Python environment compatibility for pytest**\n\n**Planning report generation in workspace output directory**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bdc7c24c87d292adf6b4f6526e11\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning minimal local pytest shim**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Evaluating minimal pytest shim feasibility**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering Python environment compatibility for pytest**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning report generation in workspace output directory**\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"The env here is missing both `python` and the `pytest` module, so I can’t execute the exact host-path command literally in this container. I did verify the fix with a direct `python3` import/run against the same package paths, and I’m writing the requested report now with the exact verification command to run in a full env.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bdd2fe7487d28ba7b4d5719a9bc4\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AgevMRGZwbRFzfP6kdtsUh0U|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bde0db2487d2920cb153ab64606b","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n`catalog` moved product prices from a top-level `price_cents` field to `price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`.\n\n`orders.adapter` still assumed the old shape:\n- `price_cents(product)` read `product.price_cents` or `dict['price_cents']`\n- `currency(product)` read top-level `currency`\n\nThat broke cross-package use with new `catalog.Product` objects and also hid non-USD currencies stored under `product.price.currency`.\n\n## Changed files\n- `/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n\n## What changed\nUpdated the `orders` adapter boundary to support both interfaces:\n- new objects with `price.amount_cents` and `price.currency`\n- dicts with nested `price`\n- legacy dicts with `price_cents` and top-level `currency`\n\nThis keeps the `Money` model in `catalog`, preserves legacy product dict support, and lets existing mixed-currency validation in `orders.service` keep raising `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`.\n\n## Verification\nPrimary command:\n```bash\ncd /workspace/in/shopmono && python3 -m pytest tests\n```\n\nThe current container image does not have the `pytest` module installed, so I verified behavior with a direct Python run using the package paths:\n```bash\ncd /workspace/in/shopmono && PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom catalog.pricing import sample_catalog\nfrom orders.service import price_order\nfrom reports.monthly import summarize_orders\n\ncatalog = sample_catalog()\nassert price_order([{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 2}, {'sku': 'PAD', 'quantity': 1}], catalog) == {'total_cents': 550, 'currency': 'USD'}\nassert summarize_orders([\n    {'id': 'o1', 'lines': [{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 2}]},\n    {'id': 'o2', 'lines': [{'sku': 'MUG', 'quantity': 1}]},\n], catalog) == {'order_count': 2, 'revenue_by_currency': {'USD': 250, 'EUR': 700}}\ntry:\n    price_order([{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 1}, {'sku': 'MUG', 'quantity': 1}], catalog)\nexcept ValueError as exc:\n    assert 'mixed' in str(exc)\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError('expected mixed-currency order to fail')\nPY\n```\n"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7gDBahwIxbR1aydyhTRg348V|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bde0db3887d292bc281289464207","name":"todo","arguments":{"action":"update","id":"TODO-f292d6b8","status":"completed","body":"Completed fix for Money interface regression by updating /workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py to support new Product.price Money and legacy price_cents dicts. Verified behavior with direct python3 run because this container lacks pytest. Wrote report to /workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":796,"output":1393,"cacheRead":20480,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":610,"totalTokens":22669,"cost":{"input":0.00199,"output":0.020895,"cacheRead":0.0051199999999999996,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.028005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198342775,"responseId":"resp_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bdc71fa487d28e922ec838bd4b44","rawStopReason":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call_AgevMRGZwbRFzfP6kdtsUh0U|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bde0db2487d2920cb153ab64606b","toolName":"write","args":{"path":"/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n`catalog` moved product prices from a top-level `price_cents` field to `price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`.\n\n`orders.adapter` still assumed the old shape:\n- `price_cents(product)` read `product.price_cents` or `dict['price_cents']`\n- `currency(product)` read top-level `currency`\n\nThat broke cross-package use with new `catalog.Product` objects and also hid non-USD currencies stored under `product.price.currency`.\n\n## Changed files\n- `/workspace/in/shopmono/packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n\n## What changed\nUpdated the `orders` adapter boundary to support both interfaces:\n- new objects with `price.amount_cents` and `price.currency`\n- dicts with nested `price`\n- legacy dicts with `price_cents` and top-level `currency`\n\nThis keeps the `Money` model in `catalog`, preserves legacy product dict support, and lets existing mixed-currency validation in `orders.service` keep raising `ValueError(\"mixed currencies are not supported\")`.\n\n## Verification\nPrimary command:\n```bash\ncd /workspace/in/shopmono && python3 -m pytest tests\n```\n\nThe current container image does not have the `pytest` module installed, so I verified behavior with a direct Python run using the package paths:\n```bash\ncd /workspace/in/shopmono && PYTHONPATH=packages/catalog:packages/orders:packages/reports python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom catalog.pricing import sample_catalog\nfrom orders.service import price_order\nfrom reports.monthly import summarize_orders\n\ncatalog = sample_catalog()\nassert price_order([{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 2}, {'sku': 'PAD', 'quantity': 1}], catalog) == {'total_cents': 550, 'currency': 'USD'}\nassert summarize_orders([\n    {'id': 'o1', 'lines': [{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 2}]},\n    {'id': 'o2', 'lines': [{'sku': 'MUG', 'quantity': 1}]},\n], catalog) == {'order_count': 2, 'revenue_by_currency': {'USD': 250, 'EUR': 700}}\ntry:\n    price_order([{'sku': 'PEN', 'quantity': 1}, {'sku': 'MUG', 'quantity': 1}], catalog)\nexcept ValueError as exc:\n    assert 'mixed' in str(exc)\nelse:\n    raise AssertionError('expected mixed-currency order to fail')\nPY\n```\n"}}
