{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The monorepo at `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/104-083-monorepo-interface-repair-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-134422-3a10d38b/workspace/in/shopmono` has a cross-package interface regression.\n\n`catalog` recently migrated product prices from the old integer `price_cents` field to a `Money(amount_cents, currency)` object. The `orders` and `reports` packages still contain old assumptions and the integration tests fail.\n\nYour job:\n- Run `python -m pytest tests` from `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/104-083-monorepo-interface-repair-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-134422-3a10d38b/workspace/in/shopmono`.\n- Repair the cross-package compatibility issue while preserving the new `catalog` model.\n- Keep support for legacy product dictionaries that still contain `price_cents`.\n- Preserve currency validation: mixed currencies in one order must raise a clear error.\n- Write `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/104-083-monorepo-interface-repair-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-134422-3a10d38b/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md` with the root cause, changed files, and verification command.\n\nConstraints:\n- Do not modify files under `<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/104-083-monorepo-interface-repair-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-134422-3a10d38b/workspace/in/shopmono/tests`.\n- Do not hard-code fixture SKUs, order ids, or customer names.\n- Do not remove the `Money` model or flatten all prices back into bare integers.\n- Do not ignore currency values or silently coerce every currency to USD.\n- Do not add third-party dependencies.\n"}],"timestamp":1788198267952},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Planning workflow inspection and architecture review**\n\n**Listing workflows and inspecting test inputs**","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd7ea11087d2946522d45dd3fc2a\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"<PROVIDER_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD_REDACTED>\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning workflow inspection and architecture review**\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Listing workflows and inspecting test inputs**\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mRjb7Si4mQOvHYTxrN5q4Jr8|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd8636ec87d289bd38945e0509e2","name":"workflow","arguments":{"action":"list","format":"json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QK1gBX2UZfKfFY2lDg7QupFu|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd8636fc87d297e8cf2522100001","name":"find","arguments":{"paths":["<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/104-083-monorepo-interface-repair-atomic-a03-r01/hb-work/atomic/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-134422-3a10d38b/workspace/in/shopmono/*"],"limit":200,"gitignore":true,"hidden":true}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_vuHJm04qPlEWqvTVo7dG7hKE|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd86370487d285c7c6757870fb11","name":"todo","arguments":{"action":"create","title":"Repair shopmono cross-package Money interface regression","status":"in_progress","tags":["bugfix","monorepo","tests"],"body":"Goal: fix cross-package compatibility after catalog price migration to Money(amount_cents, currency), preserve legacy price_cents support, keep mixed-currency validation, avoid test changes, then write report and verify with pytest."}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":971,"output":421,"cacheRead":12800,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":166,"totalTokens":14192,"cost":{"input":0.0024275000000000004,"output":0.006315,"cacheRead":0.0031999999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0119425}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788198267957,"responseId":"resp_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd7dc13087d29e66c75661b3cea3","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mRjb7Si4mQOvHYTxrN5q4Jr8|fc_067ccd0f23a21abe016a95bd8636ec87d289bd38945e0509e2","toolName":"workflow","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"action\": \"list\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"adversarial-verification\",\n      \"description\": \"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"task\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"verifier_count\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_repairs\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"accept_mean\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"reask_limit\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"classify-and-act\",\n      \"description\": \"Classify a task with structured confidence, route deterministically to an isolated category action, and ask for human selection when confidence is low.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"categories\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"confidence_threshold\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"fan-out-and-synthesize\",\n      \"description\": \"Partition a task, run bounded independent artifact branches, then synthesize all evidence at an explicit barrier.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_branches\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"generate-and-filter\",\n      \"description\": \"Generate more independent candidates than needed, deduplicate and filter them by rubric, optionally judge them, and return a parent-consumable shortlist.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_candidates\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"shortlist_size\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"use_judge\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"goal\",\n      \"description\": \"Goal Runner workflow with bounded sub-agent orchestration turns, immutable acceptance criteria, ledger artifacts, parallel reviewers, and reducer-gated completion. When launching follow-up goal runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the objective text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"objective\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_turns\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"loop-until-done\",\n      \"description\": \"Repeat evidence-producing work and independent completion evaluation against a durable ledger until done or an inspectable iteration-limit failure.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_iterations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_scoring\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"progress_repeats\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"open-claude-design\",\n      \"description\": \"AI-powered design workflow: combined discovery/init → design-system/reference research → curated reference discovery → HTML generation → one live review session → rich HTML handoff. The discovery stage asks what to build, the output type, and which references to emulate, then runs impeccable init for PRODUCT.md/DESIGN.md (references take precedence over project context). The user reviews the generated HTML in one live session.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"discover_references\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"ralph\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw prompt → research-prompt-refinement → research → orchestrate → multi-model parallel review loop with bounded iteration and immutable acceptance criteria. When launching follow-up ralph runs from review findings, pass the ORIGINAL task text as acceptance_criteria so deltas cannot drift from the literal contract. If the task includes submitting a pull request (or MR/review), remove that final action from the prompt text and set create_pr=true instead when preparing the workflow inputs.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"acceptance_criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_loops\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"base_branch\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"git_worktree_dir\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"create_pr\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"tournament\",\n      \"description\": \"Run independent whole-task attempts through a soft-scored pivot-pairing schedule and return an auditable ranking.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prompt\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"num_attempts\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"max_concurrency\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"n_evaluations\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"pivots\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"seed\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"criteria\",\n          \"required\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"models\",\n          \"required\": false\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"action":"list","items":[{"name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Produce a candidate, score independent per-criterion verifier reports, and apply a deterministic mean-and-veto gate with bounded repairs.","inputs":[{"name":"task","required":true},{"name":"verifier_count","required":false},{"name":"max_repairs","required":false},{"name":"criteria","required":false},{"name":"accept_mean","required":false},{"name":"reask_limit","required":false}]},{"name":"classify-and-act","description":"Classify a task with structured conf